<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han Dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eastern Han</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Han Dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 202 BCE to 220 CE, with a brief interruption, and is regarded as a formative era of Chinese civilisation. It consolidated centralised bureaucratic government, Confucian state ideology and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade. It has its own profile on the site and was the main rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a> on the northern frontier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/han-dynasty.jpg" alt="Han Dynasty" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DannamEmpire · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Han_Dynasty_2_BC_(cropped).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
